# Keeps out everything that is not code, notebooks, figures, the saved
# per-patch predictions or the synthetic data generator.
#
# The leading slashes matter. A bare `data/` matches a directory called `data`
# at ANY depth, which silently excluded `vmlevaluator/data/` -- the package's
# own data-loading module -- from the first commit, leaving a repository that
# could not be imported. Anchor anything that is meant to mean "the one at the
# top level".
#
# Two exclusions are deliberate and easy to "fix" by mistake:
#   * weights are NOT in the repository. They are ~600 MB, and REPRODUCE.md
#     tells a reviewer the pipeline can be checked without them, and run end to
#     end on synthetic data. If you ever publish them, link the archive from
#     README.md rather than committing them here.
#   * /data/ holds histology that is not distributable, and the human
#     predictions carry study codes -- see RELEASING.md before pushing.

# Histology and workbooks (the top-level folder only)
/data/

# Trained weights and the bundled ImageNet checkpoint
*.pth
*.joblib
/pretrained/

# Generated stand-in data and everything a re-run writes
/data_synthetic/
/runs/

# Notebook state -- notebooks/ is committed clean, notebooks/executed with outputs
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Python (these are meant to match at any depth)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
/build/
/dist/
/.venv/
/venv/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
